---
// LocalStack · Lesson 7 — Terraform II: full stack (Lambda + API GW v1 + DynamoDB) + RDS note.
import Lesson from "../../../../layouts/Lesson.astro";
const titlePt = "LocalStack 7 — Terraform II";
const titleEn = "LocalStack 7 — Terraform II";
const titleFallback = "LocalStack 7 — Terraform II";
const bodyClass = "lang-pt";
const viewport = "width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0";
const assets = [
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/style.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/dark.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/i18n.css\" />",
	"<script src=\"../assets/i18n.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/nav.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/reading-ui.js\" defer></script>",
];
---
<Lesson
	titlePt={titlePt}
	titleEn={titleEn}
	titleFallback={titleFallback}
	bodyClass={bodyClass}
	viewport={viewport}
	assets={assets}
>
	<Fragment is:raw>
    <article class="lesson">
      <header class="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow">⬡ LocalStack · Lição 7 · Difícil</span>
        <h1>
          <span data-lang="pt">Capstone: uma API completa em um apply</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Capstone: a whole API in one apply</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lead">
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Lambda (TypeScript) + API Gateway + DynamoDB, tudo declarado em
            HCL e testável com <code>curl</code>. É <strong>o desenho que
            sustenta entrevistas e projetos reais</strong> — e cabe num
            arquivo.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >Lambda (TypeScript) + API Gateway + DynamoDB, all declared in
            HCL and testable with <code>curl</code>. It is <strong>the design
            that carries interviews and real projects</strong> — and fits in
            one file.</span
          >
        </p>
      </header>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">1</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">O desenho: pedido → rota → função → tabela</span
        ><span data-lang="en">The design: request → route → function → table</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Três recursos e as ligações entre eles: o <strong>API Gateway
          (v1)</strong> expõe HTTP, a <strong>Lambda</strong> responde, o
          <strong>DynamoDB</strong> persiste. Permissões via IAM role —
          igual à lição 3, agora em HCL.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Three resources and the wiring between them: <strong>API Gateway
          (v1)</strong> exposes HTTP, the <strong>Lambda</strong> responds,
          <strong>DynamoDB</strong> persists. Permissions via IAM role —
          like lesson 3, now in HCL.</span
        >
      </p>
      <div class="callout warn">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Use <strong>API Gateway v1 (REST)</strong> — a v2 (HTTP API)
          <strong>é paga</strong> no LocalStack. No mundo real as duas
          existem; aqui, a v1 basta.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >Use <strong>API Gateway v1 (REST)</strong> — v2 (HTTP API)
          <strong>is paid</strong> on LocalStack. Both exist in the real
          world; here, v1 suffices.</span
        >
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">2</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">O HCL completo (copiável)</span
        ><span data-lang="en">The complete HCL (copyable)</span>
      </h2>
      <pre class="block"><code><span class="c"># main.tf — capstone</span>
<span class="k">terraform</span> {
  required_providers {
    aws = { source = <span class="s">"hashicorp/aws"</span>, version = <span class="s">"~&gt; 5.0"</span> }
  }
}
<span class="k">provider</span> <span class="s">"aws"</span> { region = <span class="s">"us-east-1"</span> }

<span class="c"># ---------- dados: a tabela</span>
<span class="k">resource</span> <span class="s">"aws_dynamodb_table"</span> <span class="s">"visitas"</span> {
  name         = <span class="s">"visitas"</span>
  billing_mode = <span class="s">"PAY_PER_REQUEST"</span>
  hash_key     = <span class="s">"path"</span>
  attribute {
    name = <span class="s">"path"</span>
    type = <span class="s">"S"</span>
  }
}

<span class="c"># ---------- permissões: a role da função</span>
<span class="k">data</span> <span class="s">"aws_iam_policy_document"</span> <span class="s">"assume"</span> {
  statement {
    actions = [<span class="s">"sts:AssumeRole"</span>]
    principals {
      type        = <span class="s">"Service"</span>
      identifiers = [<span class="s">"lambda.amazonaws.com"</span>]
    }
  }
}
<span class="k">resource</span> <span class="s">"aws_iam_role"</span> <span class="s">"api"</span> {
  name               = <span class="s">"api-role"</span>
  assume_role_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.assume.json
}
<span class="k">data</span> <span class="s">"aws_iam_policy_document"</span> <span class="s">"dynamo"</span> {
  statement {
    actions   = [<span class="s">"dynamodb:PutItem"</span>, <span class="s">"dynamodb:GetItem"</span>]
    resources = [aws_dynamodb_table.visitas.arn]
  }
}
<span class="k">resource</span> <span class="s">"aws_iam_role_policy"</span> <span class="s">"dynamo"</span> {
  name   = <span class="s">"dynamo"</span>
  role   = aws_iam_role.api.id
  policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.dynamo.json
}

<span class="c"># ---------- computação: a função (TS da lição 4)</span>
<span class="k">resource</span> <span class="s">"aws_lambda_function"</span> <span class="s">"api"</span> {
  function_name = <span class="s">"visitas-api"</span>
  runtime       = <span class="s">"nodejs20.x"</span>
  handler       = <span class="s">"index.handler"</span>
  role          = aws_iam_role.api.arn
  filename      = <span class="s">"function-ts.zip"</span>   <span class="c"># esbuild da lição 4</span>
  source_code_hash = filebase64sha256(<span class="s">"function-ts.zip"</span>)
  environment {
    variables = { TABLE = aws_dynamodb_table.visitas.name }
  }
}

<span class="c"># ---------- HTTP: API Gateway v1 (REST)</span>
<span class="k">resource</span> <span class="s">"aws_api_gateway_rest_api"</span> <span class="s">"api"</span> {
  name = <span class="s">"visitas-api"</span>
}
<span class="k">resource</span> <span class="s">"aws_api_gateway_resource"</span> <span class="s">"visita"</span> {
  rest_api_id = aws_api_gateway_rest_api.api.id
  parent_id   = aws_api_gateway_rest_api.api.root_resource_id
  path_part   = <span class="s">"visita"</span>
}
<span class="k">resource</span> <span class="s">"aws_api_gateway_method"</span> <span class="s">"get"</span> {
  rest_api_id   = aws_api_gateway_rest_api.api.id
  resource_id   = aws_api_gateway_resource.visita.id
  http_method   = <span class="s">"GET"</span>
  authorization = <span class="s">"NONE"</span>
}
<span class="k">resource</span> <span class="s">"aws_api_gateway_integration"</span> <span class="s">"lambda"</span> {
  rest_api_id             = aws_api_gateway_rest_api.api.id
  resource_id             = aws_api_gateway_resource.visita.id
  http_method             = aws_api_gateway_method.get.http_method
  integration_http_method = <span class="s">"POST"</span>
  type                    = <span class="s">"AWS_PROXY"</span>
  uri                     = aws_lambda_function.api.invoke_arn
}
<span class="k">resource</span> <span class="s">"aws_lambda_permission"</span> <span class="s">"apigw"</span> {
  statement_id  = <span class="s">"AllowAPIInvoke"</span>
  action        = <span class="s">"lambda:InvokeFunction"</span>
  function_name = aws_lambda_function.api.function_name
  principal     = <span class="s">"apigateway.amazonaws.com"</span>
  source_arn    = <span class="s">"</span>${aws_api_gateway_rest_api.api.execution_arn}<span class="s">/*/*"</span>
}
<span class="k">resource</span> <span class="s">"aws_api_gateway_deployment"</span> <span class="s">"api"</span> {
  depends_on = [aws_api_gateway_integration.lambda]
  rest_api_id = aws_api_gateway_rest_api.api.id
}
<span class="k">resource</span> <span class="s">"aws_api_gateway_stage"</span> <span class="s">"dev"</span> {
  rest_api_id   = aws_api_gateway_rest_api.api.id
  deployment_id = aws_api_gateway_deployment.api.id
  stage_name    = <span class="s">"dev"</span>
}

<span class="k">output</span> <span class="s">"url"</span> {
  value = <span class="s">"http://</span>${aws_api_gateway_rest_api.api.id}<span class="s">.execute-api.localhost.localstack.cloud:4566/dev/visita"</span>
}</code></pre>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >O handler grava e conta visitas — <strong>duas linguagens,
          escolha uma</strong> (o desafio pede a outra):</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >The handler records and counts visits — <strong>two languages,
          pick one</strong> (the challenge asks for the other):</span
        >
      </p>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>index.ts (deploy)</h3>
          <pre class="block"><code><span class="c">// npx esbuild index.ts --bundle --platform=node \</span>
<span class="c">//   --format=esm --outfile=index.mjs &amp;&amp; \</span>
<span class="c">//   zip -j function-ts.zip index.mjs</span>
<span class="k">import</span> { DynamoDBClient, UpdateItemCommand }
  <span class="k">from</span> <span class="s">"@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb"</span>;

<span class="k">const</span> db = <span class="k">new</span> DynamoDBClient({
  endpoint: <span class="s">"http://localhost:4566"</span>,
  region: <span class="s">"us-east-1"</span>,
  credentials: {
    accessKeyId: <span class="s">"test"</span>,
    secretAccessKey: <span class="s">"test"</span> },
});

<span class="k">export const</span> handler = <span class="k">async</span> (event: <span class="k">any</span>) <span class="k">=&gt;</span> {
  <span class="k">const</span> path = event.queryStringParameters?.caminho
    ?? <span class="s">"/"</span>;
  <span class="k">const</span> r = <span class="k">await</span> db.send(<span class="k">new</span> UpdateItemCommand({
    TableName: process.env.TABLE!,
    Key: { path: { S: path } },
    UpdateExpression: <span class="s">"ADD visitas :um"</span>,
    ExpressionAttributeValues: { <span class="s">":um"</span>: { N: <span class="s">"1"</span> } },
    ReturnValues: <span class="s">"UPDATED_NEW"</span>,
  }));
  <span class="k">return</span> {
    statusCode: 200,
    headers: { <span class="s">"content-type"</span>: <span class="s">"application/json"</span> },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      caminho: path,
      visitas: r.Attributes?.visitas?.N }),
  };
};
<span class="k">export default</span> handler;</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>index.py (alternativa)</h3>
          <pre class="block"><code><span class="k">import</span> json, os, boto3

db = boto3.client(<span class="s">"dynamodb"</span>,
    endpoint_url=<span class="s">"http://localhost:4566"</span>)

<span class="k">def</span> handler(event, context):
    path = event.get(<span class="s">"queryStringParameters"</span>,
                     {}).get(<span class="s">"caminho"</span>, <span class="s">"/"</span>)
    r = db.update_item(
        TableName=os.environ[<span class="s">"TABLE"</span>],
        Key={<span class="s">"path"</span>: {<span class="s">"S"</span>: path}},
        UpdateExpression=<span class="s">"ADD visitas :um"</span>,
        ExpressionAttributeValues={
            <span class="s">":um"</span>: {<span class="s">"N"</span>: <span class="s">"1"</span>}},
        ReturnValues=<span class="s">"UPDATED_NEW"</span>)
    <span class="k">return</span> {
        <span class="s">"statusCode"</span>: 200,
        <span class="s">"headers"</span>: {
            <span class="s">"content-type"</span>: <span class="s">"application/json"</span>},
        <span class="s">"body"</span>: json.dumps({
            <span class="s">"caminho"</span>: path,
            <span class="s">"visitas"</span>: r[<span class="s">"Attributes"</span>]
                [<span class="s">"visitas"</span>][<span class="s">"N"</span>]})}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">3</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Desafio (difícil): a stack viva + port para a outra linguagem</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Challenge (hard): the live stack + port to the other language</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="callout key">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          ><strong>Objetivo:</strong> apply único, <code>curl</code> duas
          vezes no mesmo caminho, contador sobe; depois <strong>porte o
          handler para a linguagem que você não usou</strong> (mude
          <code>runtime</code>, <code>handler</code>, <code>filename</code>) e
          re-aplique — <strong>sem apagar a tabela</strong>.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          ><strong>Goal:</strong> single apply, <code>curl</code> the same
          path twice, counter goes up; then <strong>port the handler to the
          language you did not use</strong> (change
          <code>runtime</code>, <code>handler</code>, <code>filename</code>)
          and re-apply — <strong>without deleting the table</strong>.</span
        >
      </div>
      <pre class="block"><code>tflocal init &amp;&amp; tflocal apply -auto-approve
<span class="c"># espere: Apply complete! (13~ recursos)</span>

curl <span class="s">"&lt;URL do output&gt;?caminho=/home"</span>; echo
curl <span class="s">"&lt;URL do output&gt;?caminho=/home"</span>; echo
<span class="c"># esperado / expected:</span>
<span class="s">{"caminho":"/home","visitas":"1"}</span>
<span class="s">{"caminho":"/home","visitas":"2"}</span>

<span class="c"># a prova da persistência fora da API:</span>
awslocal dynamodb get-item --table-name visitas \
  --key <span class="s">'{"path":{"S":"/home"}}'</span>
<span class="c"># esperado: Item com visitas N=2</span></code></pre>
      <div class="callout tip">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >DNS falhou no <code>execute-api.localhost…</code>? Use o formato
          alternativo do LocalStack:
          <code>http://localhost:4566/_aws/execute-api/&lt;apiId&gt;/dev/visita</code>.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >DNS failed on <code>execute-api.localhost…</code>? Use
          LocalStack's alternative form:
          <code>http://localhost:4566/_aws/execute-api/&lt;apiId&gt;/dev/visita</code>.</span
        >
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">4</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">E o RDS? (nota honesta)</span
        ><span data-lang="en">What about RDS? (honest note)</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >RDS <strong>não está no plano Community</strong> do LocalStack
          (licença paga). Para um banco relacional grátis no seu Docker,
          rode um container Postgres/MariaDB ao lado e aponte sua Lambda
          para ele por conexão normal. DynamoDB cobre o caso NoSQL — e é o
          que este capstone usa.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >RDS <strong>is not in LocalStack's Community plan</strong> (paid
          license). For a free relational DB in Docker, run a
          Postgres/MariaDB container next to it and point your Lambda at it
          with a plain connection. DynamoDB covers the NoSQL case — which is
          what this capstone uses.</span
        >
      </p>
      <p class="cite">
        <a href="https://docs.localstack.cloud/aws/services/apigateway/">API Gateway no LocalStack</a> ·
        <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/set-up-lambda-proxy-integrations.html">AWS · Lambda proxy integration</a> ·
        <a href="https://www.localstack.cloud/pricing-comparison">planos LocalStack</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">5</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Recupere sem pistas</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Retrieve without clues</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">Qual a cadeia de um GET /visita?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">What is the chain for GET /visita?</span>
          </summary>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt">API GW (method+integration AWS_PROXY) →
            Lambda (role com dynamodb:*) → tabela.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">API GW (method+AWS_PROXY integration) →
            Lambda (role with dynamodb:*) → table.</span
          >
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">Por que AWS_PROXY?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Why AWS_PROXY?</span>
          </summary>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt">Passa a requisição inteira ao handler e
            mapeia o retorno direto para a resposta HTTP.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Forwards the whole request to the handler
            and maps the return directly to the HTTP response.</span
            >
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">O que faz a aws_lambda_permission aqui?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">What does aws_lambda_permission do here?</span>
          </summary>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt">Autoriza o API Gateway a invocar a
            função.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Authorizes API Gateway to invoke the
            function.</span
            >
          </p>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">RDS no Community?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">RDS on Community?</span>
          </summary>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt">Não — pago. Alternativa grátis: container
            Postgres/MariaDB próprio.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">No — paid. Free alternative: your own
            Postgres/MariaDB container.</span
            >
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <footer class="lesson-foot">
        <div>
          <span data-lang="pt">Fonte primária:</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Primary source:</span>
          <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/set-up-lambda-proxy-integrations.html"
            >AWS · API Gateway Lambda proxy</a
          >
        </div>
